  "limitations": [
    "One local run per approach, on different dates; machine load and thermal conditions can vary.",
    "CmdStan estimates assume the 16 selected cells represent full-grid cost at 14 workers.",
    "Batch scaling repeats observed startup/drain overhead; ideal load balance assumes workers remain occupied.",
    "CmdStan uses four independent NUTS chains with 1000 warmup plus 1000 retained draws each; affine uses one 128-walker ensemble with 128 burn-in plus 256 retained sweeps.",
    "Stan generates state trajectories and writes CSV; affine computes analytic marginal/anchored trend moments from 2048 selected parameter draws.",
    "This driver schedules single-chain CmdStan subprocesses through Python threads, not MPI; MPI rank-0 NetCDF aggregation is not timed.",
    "The CmdStan setup/body timers exclude interpreter imports. Compilation is charged once, not multiplied by 19.5.",
    "Ratios compare configured workflows, not matched ESS, convergence, output contracts, precision or pure GPU acceleration.",
    "ESS projections are linear estimates from 16 cells using different ESS estimators; affine ESS/MCSE is provisional and tail ESS is not compared.",
    "The tiny 2-warmup/2-draw pipeline pilot is excluded from these measurements."
  ]
